From: ebg-ant <296364998+ebg-ant@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 17:03:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] test(mac-shell): trace-demo lets its window go over a
 Desktop that has room

The two docked windows have taken all there was, so the drag "out onto the
Desktop" went to 0 0 and the window stayed docked. A layout line that names the
Desktop gives it room, as Arbor ships.
---
 scripts/mac-shell/trace-demo.sh | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/scripts/mac-shell/trace-demo.sh b/scripts/mac-shell/trace-demo.sh
index 1bcbdf0f..f200571b 100755
--- a/scripts/mac-shell/trace-demo.sh
+++ b/scripts/mac-shell/trace-demo.sh
@@ -168,6 +168,9 @@ fi
 
 tw front "$W3"
 if pressable "$W3"; then
+  # The two docked windows have taken all there was. A layout line that names the Desktop gives it room, as Arbor ships: a place to let a window go over.
+  ctl layout "$W3 | Desktop | $W2"
+  sleep 0.5
   read -r x y <<< "$(titlebar_of "$W3")"
   read -r dx dy dw dh <<< "$(arbor_ask desktop)"
   trace_on drag-out "a docked window is dragged by its title bar out onto the Desktop and released"
